                <pb facs="0827" n="731" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg731"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.00/1263: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Hammond</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-08-25T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 25,
                                1926—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>40. Your telegram No. 60, August 15, 1 p.m. As the American Government has
                    disclaimed repeatedly any political interest or responsibility in Morocco, it is
                    now not in a position to make any comment upon the Spanish proposal that Tangier
                    be united with the existing Spanish sphere of influence in Morocco.</p>
                <p>If the other powers who are signatories of the Act of Algeciras proceed to
                    consider this suggestion, the United States would be inclined to reexamine in a
                    sympathetic spirit the matter of its future position in Morocco.</p>
                <p>The Department has received information indicating that in this instance the
                    Spanish Government is endeavoring to secure American support for use in its
                    negotiations with the other powers who are signatories of the Act of Algeciras.
                    This Government, while willing to deal with Moroccan problems in a friendly
                    spirit, does not intend to allow itself to be used in support of any particular
                    political thesis. Send copies by mail to London, Paris, Rome, and Tangier.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
